[Objective]:

Create two files; `/tmp/pwn` & `/tmp/college`. Then run `/challenge/run` for the flag.

[Key Concept]:

The `touch` command is one of the many ways to make linux files. The way this command works is by calling it, and providing the name that you want the file to be named as an argument. For example: `touch example` would create a file named example in the current working directory.

[Solution]:

Use the touch command for both files, first run `touch /tmp/pwn`, then run `touch /tmp/college`. Lastly run /challenge/run for the flag.

[# Relevant command(s) or code]:

The `touch` command creates new blank files and the argument passed to it is what the name of the file will be.

